    "location": "app/static/loader.js (minified third-party bundle); .gitignore:1; README.md",
    "description": "app/static/loader.js is a large minified Closure-library bundle with no accompanying upstream source, version metadata or checksum, so it could not be meaningfully reviewed and was excluded from manual analysis. The repository also has almost no hygiene scaffolding: .gitignore excludes only venv/*, the README is three lines and documents no security configuration, and there is no dependency manifest lock, no license attribution for the bundle and no test suite beyond the ZAP driver.",
    "impact": "An unversioned minified bundle served from the static directory can carry undisclosed vulnerabilities or be swapped without a diff anyone would notice, and it executes in every visitor's browser. Missing hygiene controls make it easy for local configuration, key material or database files to be committed, which has already happened once at F-11.",
