    "description": "One module-level connection is created at import with check_same_thread=False, explicitly disabling the guard that exists to prevent exactly this. Every concurrent request then executes statements and reads cursors through the same connection object, with no locking and no per-request transaction boundary.",
    "impact": "Under concurrency, requests interleave on a shared cursor and transaction state, producing inconsistent or wrong results, \"database is locked\" failures, partially committed writes, and in the worst case one request reading data from another request's transaction. It is also a straightforward denial-of-service vector: one slow or aborted request blocks the others.",
